# Code owners. GitHub asks the owner to review every pull request that touches these paths, and the branch
# ruleset on master requires that approval before a merge ("Require review from Code Owners"). The last matching
# line wins.
#
# The owner is the account named below. Every member is a code owner of every path, so
# keep it to the people who review code, or name a smaller child team here instead. The same team is the required
# reviewer of the mirror-production environments, where a member who did not start a deployment approves it. So
# the team needs at least two people, each with write access to the repository. A team without write access is
# silently ignored, and nobody is asked to review.
# A review covers pull requests only. A push ruleset on the path .github/** (every branch, bypass for this team
# and Dependabot only) stops anyone else from pushing a changed workflow or script to any branch, where a pull
# request into that branch would run it. The organization's own ruleset on master carries the pull request rules
# for every repository.
*                             @themasterishome
/infra/                       @themasterishome
/deploy/                      @themasterishome
/scripts/                     @themasterishome
/pipelines/                   @themasterishome
/.github/                     @themasterishome
/bicepconfig.json             @themasterishome
/.gitleaks.toml               @themasterishome
